+
+The current discovery chain requires a specific boundary repair, not just new
+search roots. `FileModuleManifestDiscovery.load()` currently performs a computed
+import from system; `AdapterRegistry` delegates to it; executable manifests
+under `1_adapters/` can themselves lazily import concrete adapters. Those edges
+cannot survive as system→composition or adapter→peer-adapter exceptions.
+
+Destination split for WP-04:
+
+- `platform/server/system/modules/FileModuleManifestDiscovery.mjs` enumerates
+  paths only. Route enumeration I/O through approved system FileIO as required
+  by D10; importing modules is not part of its interface.
+- `backend/src/composition/integrations/AdapterRegistry.mjs` owns module loading,
+  selection and indexing. Inject a loader for tests; production loading happens
+  in composition. `IntegrationLoader` stays in that composition area.
+- Executable provider manifests move to the owning facility's
+  `server/composition/providers/<provider>/manifest.mjs`, with public composition
+  entries where another owner loads them. For example, the OpenAI factory
+  registration belongs under `capabilities/ai/server/composition/providers/openai/`;
+  the concrete adapter remains under `capabilities/ai/server/adapters/`.
+  Data-only provider schemas stay with their owner and retain data classification.
+- Installed composition supplies the finite provider target set/discovery roots.
+  Preserve the captured discovery sequence, duplicate last-registration behavior,
+  provider ordering/defaults, config precedence, lazy adapter construction,
+  missing/invalid-manifest logging and failure/no-op behavior. A new directory
+  traversal order must not silently choose a different provider. Do not add a
+  new runtime activation catalog.
+
+Required proofs: reject a computed system import into a composition/adapter
+target; reject an executable manifest mislabeled adapter that imports a concrete
+peer; accept the corrected chain with no dynamic-import exemption; replay
+ordered/duplicate/invalid discovery and lazy construction using fake modules.
+This source split is required before relocating discovery infrastructure.
